# diff, answered by GNU diff 3.10 in the C locale. The three output styles,
# their context and label options, the whitespace and case options, binary
# files, standard input, names that need quoting, -N, and the usage errors.
# The virtual filesystem keeps no modification times, so a header carries
# the name alone, as it does under --label: what GNU printed after the tab
# was dropped when these were recorded, except the epoch stamp -N gives a
# file that does not exist, which patch reads as meaning exactly that.
# Which of several shortest change sets diff picks is its own; every case
# here has one shortest change set, so the bytes are GNU's bytes.
@tree pair
@mode readonly
diff ten ten2 => "3c3\n< c\n---\n> X\n9c9\n< i\n---\n> Y\n" 1
